.el .ds Aq '
.TH morsh 1  "morsh 0.3.0"
.SH NAME
morsh \- morsh \- Next\-generation resilient QUIC SSH client (combining Mosh & SSH3)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmorsh\fR [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-port\fR] [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-identity\fR] [\fB\-F\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-option\fR] [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-compress\fR] [\fB\-4\fR|\fB\-\-ipv4\fR] [\fB\-6\fR|\fB\-\-ipv6\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-completions\fR] [\fB\-\-man\fR] [\fB\-\-password\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-agent\fR] [\fB\-k\fR|\fB\-\-insecure\fR] [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-server\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-stealth\-knock\fR] [\fB\-\-force\-tcp\fR] [\fB\-\-tcp\-fallback\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-L\fR|\fB\-\-local\-forward\fR] [\fB\-R\fR|\fB\-\-remote\-forward\fR] [\fB\-D\fR|\fB\-\-dynamic\-forward\fR] [\fB\-U\fR|\fB\-\-udp\-forward\fR] [\fB\-N\fR|\fB\-\-no\-shell\fR] [\fB\-\-resume\fR] [\fB\-\-token\fR] [\fB\-\-list\-sessions\fR] [\fB\-\-ping\fR] [\fB\-\-predict\fR] [\fB\-\-predict\-style\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIDESTINATION\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
morsh \- Next\-generation resilient QUIC SSH client (combining Mosh & SSH3)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR \fI<PORT>\fR
Override remote port (defaults to 2222 or port from destination / config)
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-identity\fR \fI<IDENTITY>\fR
Path to SSH private key file (e.g. ~/.ssh/id_ed25519)
.TP
\fB\-F\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to alternative client configuration file (defaults to ~/.morsh/config.toml)
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-option\fR \fI<KEY=VALUE>\fR
OpenSSH compatibility options in format Option=Value
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-compress\fR
Request stream compression
.TP
\fB\-4\fR, \fB\-\-ipv4\fR
Force IPv4 address resolution only
.TP
\fB\-6\fR, \fB\-\-ipv6\fR
Force IPv6 address resolution only
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase verbosity level (\-v: info, \-vv: debug, \-vvv: trace)
.TP
\fB\-\-completions\fR \fI<SHELL>\fR
Generate shell completions for the specified shell (bash, zsh, fish) and exit
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
bash
.IP \(bu 2
elvish
.IP \(bu 2
fish
.IP \(bu 2
powershell
.IP \(bu 2
zsh
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-man\fR
Generate man page (roff format) to stdout and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-password\fR \fI<PASSWORD>\fR
Password for password / PAM authentication
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-agent\fR
Disable querying local ssh\-agent ($SSH_AUTH_SOCK)
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-insecure\fR
Accept any server certificate without validation (insecure / testing mode)
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-server\-name\fR \fI<SERVER_NAME>\fR
TLS Server Name Indication (SNI) override
.TP
\fB\-\-stealth\-knock\fR \fI<STEALTH_KNOCK>\fR
Optional stealth knock path prefix (SSH3 style anti\-scanning defense)
.TP
\fB\-\-force\-tcp\fR
Force TLS 1.3 over TCP fallback (bypasses QUIC/UDP)
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-fallback\-timeout\fR \fI<MS>\fR [default: 300]
Happy Eyeballs TCP fallback threshold in milliseconds (default: 300 ms)
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-local\-forward\fR \fI<SPEC>\fR
Local TCP port forwarding [bind_addr:]bind_port:target_host:target_port (\-L)
.TP
\fB\-R\fR, \fB\-\-remote\-forward\fR \fI<SPEC>\fR
Remote TCP port forwarding [bind_addr:]bind_port:target_host:target_port (\-R)
.TP
\fB\-D\fR, \fB\-\-dynamic\-forward\fR \fI<SPEC>\fR
Dynamic SOCKS5 proxy port [bind_addr:]bind_port (\-D)
.TP
\fB\-U\fR, \fB\-\-udp\-forward\fR \fI<SPEC>\fR
Native UDP port forwarding [bind_addr:]bind_port:target_host:target_port (\-U)
.TP
\fB\-N\fR, \fB\-\-no\-shell\fR
Do not allocate an interactive PTY shell (tunnel\-only mode)
.TP
\fB\-\-resume\fR \fI<SESSION_ID>\fR
Resume an existing detached persistent session by 128\-bit session ID (hex string)
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<TOKEN>\fR
Cryptographic 128\-bit resumption token (hex string) for session resumption
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-sessions\fR
List active persistent sessions on the server and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-ping\fR \fI<PING>\fR [default: 0]
Send N ping packets to measure round\-trip latency over QUIC (0 starts interactive terminal session)
.TP
\fB\-\-predict\fR \fI<MODE>\fR [default: auto]
Predictive local echo mode: auto, always, or never
.TP
\fB\-\-predict\-style\fR \fI<STYLE>\fR [default: underline]
Predictive local echo visual style: underline, dim, or none
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIDESTINATION\fR]
Remote destination in format [user@]host[:port]
.TP
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
Optional command to execute on remote host
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0
